@startuml error_flow_object_storage_failure

title COOKie MVP - Object Storage Failure Handling Flow\nYandex Object Storage Upload Error Scenarios

actor "Admin Client" as Client
participant "UploadController" as Controller
participant "Image Processing\nService" as ImageService
participant "Upload Service\n(IStorageService)" as UploadService
cloud "Yandex Object\nStorage (S3)" as S3
database "PostgreSQL\nimages table" as DB
participant "Hangfire\nBackground Jobs" as Queue
participant "Serilog\nLogger" as Logger
participant "Sentry\nMonitoring" as Sentry

== Scenario 1: Upload Timeout (Network Issue) ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image\nContent-Type: multipart/form-data\n(file: recipe_photo.jpg, 3.2MB)
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Validate JWT + Admin role

Controller -> ImageService: process_image(file)
activate ImageService

ImageService -> ImageService: Validate file:\n- Size: 3.2MB (OK, < 5MB)\n- Type: JPEG (OK, magic bytes FF D8 FF)\n- Dimensions: 2400x1600 (OK)

ImageService -> ImageService: Generate variants:\n- thumbnail: 200x200 (WebP)\n- medium: 800x600 (WebP)\n- large: 1600x1200 (WebP)

ImageService --> Controller: 3 image variants ready
deactivate ImageService

Controller -> UploadService: upload_variants(variants[])
activate UploadService

UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/thumbnail.webp\n(timeout: 30 seconds)
activate S3

S3 --> UploadService: Timeout after 30s\n(network connectivity issue)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "S3 upload timeout, retrying",\n  variant: "thumbnail",\n  attempt: 1,\n  timeout_ms: 30000\n)

UploadService -> UploadService: Retry attempt 1\n(delay: 2 seconds)

UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/thumbnail.webp\n(retry 1)
activate S3

S3 --> UploadService: Timeout again
deactivate S3

UploadService -> UploadService: Retry attempt 2\n(delay: 4 seconds, exponential backoff)

UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/thumbnail.webp\n(retry 2)
activate S3

S3 --> UploadService: Timeout again\n(3 retries exhausted)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> Logger: Log.Error(\n  "S3 upload failed after 3 retries",\n  variant: "thumbnail",\n  file_size: 45000,\n  total_time_ms: 96000\n)

UploadService -> UploadService: Switch to async upload strategy

UploadService -> Queue: Enqueue async upload job:\n{\n  job_type: "image_upload",\n  variants: [thumbnail, medium, large],\n  file_paths: [temp file locations],\n  retry_count: 0,\n  max_retries: 5\n}
activate Queue

Queue --> UploadService: Job ID: "job-uuid-1"
deactivate Queue

UploadService -> DB: INSERT INTO images (\n  id, status, job_id,\n  original_filename, file_size,\n  uploaded_by, created_at\n) VALUES (\n  'uuid-1', 'processing', 'job-uuid-1',\n  'recipe_photo.jpg', 3200000,\n  'admin-uuid', NOW()\n)
activate DB
DB --> UploadService: Image record created
deactivate DB

UploadService --> Controller: UploadResult {\n  image_id: "uuid-1",\n  status: "processing",\n  job_id: "job-uuid-1"\n}
deactivate UploadService

Controller --> Client: 202 Accepted\n{\n  "id": "uuid-1",\n  "status": "processing",\n  "job_id": "job-uuid-1",\n  "message": "Upload queued for processing",\n  "check_status_url": "/api/v1/upload/status/job-uuid-1"\n}
deactivate Controller

== Async Upload Job Execution ==

Queue -> UploadService: Execute upload job\n(job-uuid-1, attempt 1)
activate UploadService

UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/thumbnail.webp
activate S3

alt S3 Recovered
  S3 --> UploadService: 200 OK\nETag: "abc123"
  deactivate S3

  UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/medium.webp
  activate S3
  S3 --> UploadService: 200 OK
  deactivate S3

  UploadService -> S3: PUT /recipes/uuid-1/large.webp
  activate S3
  S3 --> UploadService: 200 OK
  deactivate S3

  UploadService -> DB: UPDATE images SET\n  status = 'completed',\n  cdn_url_thumbnail = 'https://cdn.cookie.com/...',\n  cdn_url_medium = 'https://cdn.cookie.com/...',\n  cdn_url_large = 'https://cdn.cookie.com/...'\nWHERE id = 'uuid-1'
  activate DB
  DB --> UploadService: Updated
  deactivate DB

  UploadService -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "Async upload completed",\n  image_id: "uuid-1",\n  total_variants: 3\n)
  deactivate UploadService

else S3 Still Down
  S3 --> UploadService: Error: ServiceUnavailable
  deactivate S3

  UploadService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Async upload failed, will retry",\n  attempt: 1,\n  next_retry_delay: "5 minutes"\n)

  UploadService -> Queue: Reschedule job\n(delay: 5 minutes,\n attempt: 2 of 5)
  deactivate UploadService
end

== Scenario 2: Invalid Image Format ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image\n(file: malicious.exe renamed to .jpg)
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Validate JWT + Admin role

Controller -> ImageService: process_image(file)
activate ImageService

ImageService -> ImageService: Read magic bytes:\nFirst 4 bytes: 4D 5A 90 00\n(MZ header = Windows executable)

ImageService -> ImageService: Compare with allowed formats:\n- JPEG: FF D8 FF\n- PNG: 89 50 4E 47\n- WebP: 52 49 46 46\n→ NO MATCH (invalid format)

ImageService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Invalid file upload attempt",\n  claimed_extension: ".jpg",\n  actual_magic_bytes: "4D5A9000",\n  detected_type: "application/x-msdownload",\n  admin_user: "admin-uuid"\n)

ImageService --> Controller: Throw InvalidImageFormatException(\n  "File is not a valid image"\n)
deactivate ImageService

Controller --> Client: 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/invalid-file-format",\n  "title": "Validation Failed",\n  "status": 422,\n  "detail": "File is not a valid image. Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, WebP",\n  "invalid_params": [\n    {\n      "field": "file",\n      "reason": "Invalid image format detected",\n      "allowed_formats": ["image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/webp"]\n    }\n  ]\n}
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 3: File Size Exceeds Limit ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image\n(file: huge_photo.jpg, 12MB)
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Check Content-Length: 12582912\n(> 5MB limit = 5242880 bytes)

Controller -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "Upload rejected: file too large",\n  size_bytes: 12582912,\n  max_bytes: 5242880\n)

Controller --> Client: 413 Payload Too Large\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/payload-too-large",\n  "title": "Payload Too Large",\n  "status": 413,\n  "detail": "File size 12.0MB exceeds maximum 5MB",\n  "max_size_bytes": 5242880,\n  "actual_size_bytes": 12582912\n}
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 4: Image Dimension Validation ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image\n(file: tiny_icon.png, 50x50 pixels)
activate Controller

Controller -> ImageService: process_image(file)
activate ImageService

ImageService -> ImageService: Read image metadata:\n- Width: 50px\n- Height: 50px\n- Required: min 800x600

ImageService -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "Image dimensions too small",\n  width: 50, height: 50,\n  min_width: 800, min_height: 600\n)

ImageService --> Controller: Throw InvalidImageDimensionsException
deactivate ImageService

Controller --> Client: 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/invalid-image-dimensions",\n  "title": "Validation Failed",\n  "status": 422,\n  "detail": "Image dimensions 50x50 are below minimum 800x600",\n  "invalid_params": [\n    {\n      "field": "file",\n      "reason": "Image dimensions too small",\n      "min_width": 800,\n      "min_height": 600,\n      "actual_width": 50,\n      "actual_height": 50\n    }\n  ]\n}
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 5: Partial Upload Failure (Multi-Variant) ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image\n(file: valid_photo.jpg, 2MB)
activate Controller

Controller -> ImageService: process_image(file)
activate ImageService
ImageService --> Controller: 3 variants generated
deactivate ImageService

Controller -> UploadService: upload_variants(variants[])
activate UploadService

UploadService -> S3: PUT thumbnail.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 200 OK (uploaded)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> S3: PUT medium.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 200 OK (uploaded)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> S3: PUT large.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 500 Internal Server Error\n(S3 partial failure)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Partial upload failure",\n  succeeded: ["thumbnail", "medium"],\n  failed: ["large"]\n)

UploadService -> UploadService: Retry large variant\n(3 attempts)

UploadService -> S3: PUT large.webp (retry)
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 500 Error (still failing)
deactivate S3

UploadService -> UploadService: Cleanup: delete uploaded variants\n(maintain consistency)

UploadService -> S3: DELETE thumbnail.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 204 No Content
deactivate S3

UploadService -> S3: DELETE medium.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 204 No Content
deactivate S3

UploadService -> Logger: Log.Error(\n  "Upload failed, cleaned up partial uploads",\n  cleaned_variants: ["thumbnail", "medium"]\n)

UploadService -> Queue: Enqueue full retry job\n(all 3 variants)

UploadService --> Controller: UploadResult {\n  status: "processing",\n  job_id: "job-uuid-2"\n}
deactivate UploadService

Controller --> Client: 202 Accepted\n{\n  "id": "uuid-2",\n  "status": "processing",\n  "job_id": "job-uuid-2",\n  "message": "Upload partially failed, retrying in background"\n}
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 6: Storage Quota Exceeded ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/upload/image
activate Controller

Controller -> UploadService: upload_variants(variants[])
activate UploadService

UploadService -> S3: PUT thumbnail.webp
activate S3
S3 --> UploadService: 403 Forbidden\nError: QuotaExceeded\n"Storage quota exceeded for bucket"
deactivate S3

UploadService -> Logger: Log.Critical(\n  "Storage quota exceeded!",\n  bucket: "cookie-images",\n  error: "QuotaExceeded"\n)

UploadService -> Sentry: CaptureException(\n  StorageQuotaExceededException,\n  severity: "critical"\n)

UploadService --> Controller: Throw StorageQuotaExceededException
deactivate UploadService

Controller --> Client: 503 Service Unavailable\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/storage-unavailable",\n  "title": "Service Unavailable",\n  "status": 503,\n  "detail": "Image storage temporarily unavailable",\n  "retry_after": 3600\n}
deactivate Controller

== Upload Retry Strategy ==

note over UploadService, S3
  **Synchronous Upload Retry (Polly):**
  - Max retries: 3
  - Delay: 2s, 4s, 8s (exponential backoff)
  - Timeout per attempt: 30 seconds
  - Total max time: ~45 seconds

  **Retryable Errors:**
  - TimeoutException
  - HttpRequestException (5xx)
  - OperationCanceledException

  **Non-Retryable Errors (fail immediately):**
  - 400 Bad Request (malformed)
  - 403 Forbidden (auth/quota)
  - 404 Not Found (wrong bucket)

  **Async Retry (Hangfire Background Jobs):**
  - Max retries: 5
  - Delay: 5min, 15min, 30min, 1hr, 2hr
  - Job expires: 24 hours
  - On final failure: mark image as "failed"
  - Alert admin via Sentry

  **Cleanup on Failure:**
  - Delete partially uploaded variants
  - Remove temp files from local disk
  - Update image record: status = "failed"
  - Keep image metadata for retry
end note

== Upload Status Check ==

note over Client, Controller
  **Status Check Endpoint:**

  GET /api/v1/upload/status/{job_id}

  **Possible Statuses:**
  - "processing": Upload in background queue
  - "completed": All variants uploaded successfully
  - "failed": All retries exhausted
  - "partial": Some variants uploaded (edge case)

  **Response Example:**
  {
    "job_id": "job-uuid-1",
    "status": "completed",
    "image": {
      "id": "uuid-1",
      "cdn_url_thumbnail": "https://cdn...",
      "cdn_url_medium": "https://cdn...",
      "cdn_url_large": "https://cdn..."
    },
    "completed_at": "2025-10-18T12:05:00Z"
  }
end note

